# Goodnight: when you say goodnight, or at a set time. Lights off, the
# heating down for the night, and one tap before the door is locked.
# /setup routines fills in the <...> parts with your devices. By hand: put
# your device names (from home.ini) in their place; #if blocks stay or go
# with what your home has.
workflow goodnight
subject house
about When you say goodnight (or at <goodnight at>): the lights off<night heating words><night lock words>.
start owner, schedule:goodnight-at
phrases goodnight, good night, night night
tag no
limits steps 20, days 1

step night
tools home/home_state, home/home_set
do:
  It is bedtime. Switch off every light that is on. <night heating instruction>
  Don't touch anything else. Then answer in one short sentence what you did,
  as the devices read back, with units, like: "Lights are off downstairs and
  the heating is at 18 °C." If something didn't take, say so plainly.
on fail goto night_failed

step tell
say {night}
#if lock
goto door
#end
#if !lock
end
#end

step night_failed
say The lights and the heating didn't change: {night.error}
#if !lock
end
#end
#if lock

step door
tool home/home_wait {"device": "<lock>", "property": "lock", "condition": "==", "value": "unlocked", "timeout_s": 0}
on fail goto end_night
if door has not within goto locked

step ask
approve The <lock label> is unlocked.
yes Lock it
no Leave it
timeout 30m
on deny goto left

step lock
tool home/home_guarded {"device": "<lock>", "action": "lock"}
on fail goto lock_failed
if lock starts done goto done

step unsure
say I sent it, but the <lock label> hasn't said it is locked: {lock}
end

step done
say <Lock label> locked. Good night.
end

step lock_failed
say The <lock label> didn't lock: {lock.error}
end

step left
say <Lock label> left unlocked. Good night.
end

step locked
say The <lock label> is locked. Good night.
end

step end_night
end
#end
